  "slug": "latent-ancestry-coordinates-e4f8",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a 2026 publication couple latent biological embeddings with ontology structure, LLM priors, or feature attribution.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is learning structured low-dimensional latent coordinates for biological entities and making them interpretable or constrained by prior knowledge. MEDALLION distills t-SNE and UMAP embeddings into a neural encoder and applies feature attribution to identify which original features shape the layout. scOntoFM embeds the cell ontology hierarchy via LCA-based triplet sampling to improve zero-shot cell- and gene-level performance. GeneEmbedLLM produces semantically aware gene embeddings from multi-source data using LLM-based encoding with contrastive learning. SpaMEDM combines masked reconstruction with diffusion-based latent noise prediction for multi-omics spatial domain identification. What is new is the explicit injection of ontology, language-model, or diffusion-based regularization into the latent space itself, rather than treating embeddings as opaque outputs.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-12"
}
